Harness addition: POKE / POKEOBJ / SHOT / RAM events and ANCHOR sections in the X2REF_INPUT script, so Hatari can run the same coverage-poke
recipes as x2recomp's input scripts and be timed from game events (tools/trace/make_st_replays.py --hatari, tools/compare/st_replay_compare.py).
  <vbl> POKE <addr> <value> <size>          write RAM (hex, size 1/2/4)
  <vbl> POKEOBJ <handler> <offset> <value> <size>   write into the hittable objects whose hit handler (+$A) is <handler>
  ANCHOR <level>                             the following '+<delta> <event>' lines run <delta> VBLs after the first scroll movement
                                             ($CD0 leaving $1200) once $E04 is <level>; '+<delta> SHOT' saves a screenshot, '+<delta> RAM' dumps the RAM
Applies on top of 0001-x2ref-harness.patch.

